A “transportation-infrastructure-adjacent frontage” shall refer to a #street# frontage that contains at least one of the following:

(a) an elevated rail line;

(b) an open #railroad right-of-way#;

(c) a limited-access expressway, freeway, parkway or highway, all of which prohibit direct vehicular access to adjoining land; or

(d) an elevated #street# located on a bridge.
